<div>
    <div class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <h3>Governance that enables speed while managing emerging risks</h3=
>
<p>While this is not an easy feat, Vince Campisi, chief digital officer and=
 leader of the enterprise services division at aerospace and defense compan=
y RTX, shares his strategy for adapting governance in the age of AI: =E2=80=
=9CBreak governance down into three M=E2=80=99s: map, measure, and monitor.=
 This means teams can map activities to keep tabs on progress, measure resu=
lts to see if they=E2=80=99re achieving the outcomes they want, and monitor=
 quality to make sure the initial goals are realized. Next, focus on tactic=
s designed to maintain alignment with strategic intent. As AI becomes more =
agentic, organizations can establish governance that starts with leadership=
=E2=80=99s intent and builds in explainability and auditability so humans c=
an verify and trust the results.=E2=80=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloit=
te.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends/2026/ai-futu=
re-it-function.html#endnote-24" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 24"=
>24</a></sup></p>
<h3>Bold ambition prioritizing reimagination over incremental change</h3>
<p>Transforming the tech org demands more than a series of small, safe step=
s=E2=80=94it requires a courageous vision that reimagines what=E2=80=99s po=
ssible. Organizations that set bold ambitions harness AI far beyond tactica=
l automation, radically reshaping how technology, talent, and strategy inte=
rsect.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CRather than getting stuck in a cycle of perpetual proofs of con=
cept, consider attacking your biggest problem and go for a big outcome,=E2=
=80=9D says Daniel Dines, UiPath CEO and executive chairman. =E2=80=9CWith =
a significant success in hand, you can then prove that there are not just o=
pportunities to rethink business processes but also potential productivity =
enhancements and opportunities to uncover new revenue streams. The sooner y=
ou get started, the better your position can be in the journey toward those=
 ends.=E2=80=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topi=
cs/technology-management/tech-trends/2026/ai-future-it-function.html#endnot=
e-25" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 25">25</a></sup></p>
<h3>Redefining the CIO role</h3>
<p>As AI takes hold, the CIO=E2=80=99s mandate is expanding from tech strat=
egist to AI evangelist. In fact, 70% of CIOs from the Tech Executive Survey=
 say their primary role with gen AI at their organizations is either implem=
enting gen AI across the enterprise or serving as an evangelist, helping te=
ams see the possibilities of the technology.<sup><a href=3D"https://www.del=
oitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-management/tech-trends/2026/ai-f=
uture-it-function.html#endnote-26" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number =
26">26</a></sup>&nbsp;As AI-enabled capabilities are embedded across organi=
zations and IT is less centralized, CIOs become orchestrators and integrato=
rs rather than owners of infrastructure. In fact, almost a third of CIOs sa=
y that orchestrating fellow tech leaders is essential in the next 18 months=
.<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topics/technology-=
management/tech-trends/2026/ai-future-it-function.html#endnote-27" aria-lab=
el=3D"Endnotes reference number 27">27</a></sup>&nbsp;The role now requires=
 deeper integration with business strategy and enterprisewide transformatio=
n, making the CIO both a change agent and a responsible gatekeeper.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CCIOs were once more like chief integration officers because muc=
h of their remit was making sure SaaS and other applications worked togethe=
r effectively. Today, I consider my role a combination of the traditional C=
IO plus chief data officer, chief AI officer, and chief digital officer,=E2=
=80=9D adds Western Digital=E2=80=99s Tirumala. =E2=80=9CThis era is an opp=
ortunity for technology leaders to step up. We understand the technology, t=
he data, and the processes. Don=E2=80=99t wait for permission=E2=80=94lean =
in as a partner. Articulate a strong digital ambition and develop a road ma=
p for enabling top-line growth and business model shifts, along with a stra=
tegy for managing the risks. Focus on speed, agility, outcomes, and value. =
With the right approach, there won=E2=80=99t be any need to ask for forgive=
ness later on.=E2=80=9D<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insig=
hts/topics/technology-management/tech-trends/2026/ai-future-it-function.htm=
l#endnote-28" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 28">28</a></sup></p>

    </div>
